[h1]Continuation update[/h1]
This independently maintained continuation supports RimWorld 1.6 and includes optional Combat Extended 1.6 compatibility files, dedicated ammunition, and ballistic handling. Load Combat Extended before this mod. Combat Extended is not bundled. Biotech is required. Do not enable this together with the original mod.

Released with permission from the original author; this is not the original project.

Original author: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/id/yzywd]POP[/url]
Original project: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3276521515]Pollution weapon (Abandoned)[/url]
Source repository: [url=https://github.com/Juggernautsst/PollutionArmory-Continued]PollutionArmory-Continued[/url]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Juggernautsst/PollutionArmory-Continued/main/Workshop/Images/English/compatibility.png[/img]

[h1]Original mod description (reproduced with permission)[/h1]
Do you find the task of dealing with toxic wastepack to be too mundane, with seemingly few uses for them? This series of modules was created to address this issue. It includes the addition of 3 disposable weapons and 4 “conventional weapons” that unleash skills by consuming pollution and waste.

Using this method, you can orderly control the amount of your trash. For instance, the pollution bomb needs to be detonated by humans themselves, effectively cleaning up the pollution while simultaneously eliminating some useless slaves.
Moreover, the power of these weapons corresponds to different levels of technology, with high-tech weapons offering powerful and unique abilities.

[h1]Note: This mod requires the Biotech DLC.[/h1]

